# SEO

## Every page
```typescript
import type { Metadata } from 'next'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  metadataBase: new URL('https://domain.com'),
  title: 'Primary Keyword | Brand',      // 50-60 chars
  description: 'Compelling summary.',     // 150-160 chars
  alternates: { canonical: '/page' },
  openGraph: {
    title: '...',
    description: '...',
    url: '/page',
    type: 'website',
    images: [{ url: '/og.png', width: 1200, height: 630 }],
  },
  twitter: { card: 'summary_large_image', title: '...', description: '...' },
}
```

`metadataBase` set once in the root layout makes every relative canonical and OG URL resolve absolute. Set it there, then use relative paths on pages.

Viewport and theme color go in a separate `export const viewport: Viewport`, not inside `metadata`.

## JSON-LD
- Homepage: `Organization` + `WebSite`
- Service pages: `Service`
- Every non-homepage: `BreadcrumbList`
- Articles: `Article` with `datePublished` and `author`

Render as `<script type="application/ld+json" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: JSON.stringify(schema) }} />` in the page body. Validate against schema.org before shipping — do not invent property names.

## Files
`app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts` as generated routes. Not static files in `public/`.

## Banned meta tags
`keywords` (ignored since 2009), `revisit-after` (never worked), `rating`, `generator`.

## Check
- [ ] Title 50-60 characters
- [ ] Description 150-160 characters
- [ ] Canonical resolves absolute
- [ ] OG and Twitter tags present, OG image 1200×630
- [ ] JSON-LD present and valid
- [ ] BreadcrumbList on every non-homepage
- [ ] Page appears in `sitemap.ts`
